tely. Setting up thread scope closures...\n\nThe key insight is that `move` closures will capture the references by copying them since they're `Copy` types, which is exactly what we need—the references themselves get duplicated across threads while still pointing to the same underlying data. This approach should handle both the scatter and global processing threads cleanly. I should also make sure to address that CUDA warning about `task_stride` while I'm at it.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":662,"cache_read_input_tokens":94209,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":662},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8f65911c-bec8-4486-8d04-3600a654369d","uuid":"9544c448-bb43-4d75-9ac9-4b2b5f2771ec"}
