{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01C3VpAqWqCVRns1MiBAXMfH","type":"tool_result","content":"=== Checklist ===\n\n1. Before measurements:\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-14-0830-batch-scatter-gkr-input-eval/results/before_apc000.json\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-14-0830-batch-scatter-gkr-input-eval/results/before_apc100.json\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-14-0830-batch-scatter-gkr-input-eval/results/before_apc300_r1.json\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-14-0830-batch-scatter-gkr-input-eval/results/before_apc300_r2.json\n\n2. After measurements:\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-14-0830-batch-scatter-gkr-input-eval/results/after_apc000.json\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-14-0830-batch-scatter-gkr-input-eval/results/after_apc100.json\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-14-0830-batch-scatter-gkr-input-eval/results/after_apc300_r1.json\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-14-0830-batch-scatter-gkr-input-eval/results/after_apc300_r2.json\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-14-0830-batch-scatter-gkr-input-eval/results/after_apc300_r3.json\n\n3. Report exists:\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 georg georg 6953 Apr 14 11:47 /home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-14-0830-batch-scatter-gkr-input-eval/report.md\n\n4. Log entry exists:\n\n**Result**: success — Round 0 at APC 300: 245ms → 202ms (3.28x lower vs baseline 662ms). STARK excl trace at APC 300: 1383ms → 1336ms, 1.84x lower vs baseline (vs previous: -47ms, 1.04x lower).\n\n**Summary**: Replaced per-AIR D2H sync + CPU post-processing with GPU-side matrix-vector multiply using pre-computed transformation matrices that capture the entire pipeline (transpose + iDFT + unshift + Lagrange interpolation + coefficient adjustment). Polynomial coefficients are written directly into a shared device batch array, with a single D2H copy replacing ~1246 per-AIR pipeline drains. Round 0 improved 21% at APC 300 with no regression at APC 0. The pre-computed matrix approach is simpler and more robust than implementing the Bowers iDFT on GPU.\n\n## 2026-04-14-0730-overlap-logup-precompute-round0\n\n**Idea**: Overlap logup combination precomputation (d_eq_3b upload + precompute kernels) with Round 0 multi-stream evaluation by running it on a background thread.\n\n**Result**: success — STARK excl trace at APC 300: 1370ms → 1306ms, 1.88x lower vs baseline (vs previous: -64ms, 1.05x lower). Round 0: 203ms → 182ms (-21ms, 1.12x lower).\n\n**Summary**: Spawned d_eq_3b upload + logup_combinations precompute on a background thread inside the existing thread::scope block, concurrent with Round 0 worker threads. The precompute output is only consumed during MLE rounds, making it fully independent of Round 0. Per-segment Round 0 improved by ~10ms (93ms → 82ms). LogUp GKR also improved by 44ms, likely due to improved CUDA memory pool state from overlapped allocations. No regression at APC 0 (single-threaded path unchanged).\n\n## 2026-04-14-0830-batch-scatter-gkr-input-eval\n\n**Idea**: Batch SCATTER-mode GKR input evaluation AIRs into a single descriptor-array CUDA kernel launch per segment on a dedicated background thread.\n\n**Result**: failure — LogUp GKR at APC 300: 518ms → 510ms (-8ms median, 1.02x lower vs before, below 10ms rollback threshold). STARK excl trace at APC 300: 1302ms → 1297ms (-5ms, within noise). (vs baseline: 1.89x lower, unchanged from previous)\n\n**Summary**: Implemented a batched SCATTER kernel using the descriptor-array pattern (BlockCtx + GkrInputScatterCtx), running on a dedicated background thread concurrent with 8 GLOBAL worker threads. Fixed a correctness bug where multiple lifted SCATTER AIRs shared the same tmp buffer during concurrent kernel writes (needed per-AIR offsets). The optimization produces correct proofs but the improvement (~8ms median) is below the 10ms threshold because SCATTER AIRs' aggregate GPU time (~63ms) is already hidden behind the longer GLOBAL processing (~464ms). The batching reduces CPU-side overhead per SCATTER AIR but doesn't change the GLOBAL-dominated critical path.\n\n5. Git log:\n0137c6a9 Revert \"Batch SCATTER-mode GKR input evaluation into descriptor-array kernel\"\n74078beb Batch SCATTER-mode GKR input evaluation into descriptor-array kernel\n1bfddca1 Update results\n\n6. Git tag:\nautoopt/2026-04-14-0030-rightsize-gkr-input-kernel-grid\nautoopt/2026-04-14-0140-multistream-stacked-reduction-round0\nautoopt/2026-04-14-0300-precompute-logup-round0-interaction-rules\nautoopt/2026-04-14-0330-gpu-round0-poly-extraction\nautoopt/2026-04-14-0730-overlap-logup-precompute-round0\nautoopt/2026-04-14-0830-batch-scatter-gkr-input-eval\n\n7. autoopt-results NOT committed:\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-0030-rightsize-gkr-input-kernel-grid/plan.md\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-0030-rightsize-gkr-input-kernel-grid/report.md\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-0030-rightsize-gkr-input-kernel-grid/results/after_apc000.json\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-0030-rightsize-gkr-input-kernel-grid/results/after_apc100.json\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-0030-rightsize-gkr-input-kernel-grid/results/after_apc300.json\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-0030-rightsize-gkr-input-kernel-grid/results/after_apc300_run2.json\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-0030-rightsize-gkr-input-kernel-grid/results/before_apc000.json\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-0030-rightsize-gkr-input-kernel-grid/results/before_apc100.json\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-0030-rightsize-gkr-input-kernel-grid/results/before_apc300.json\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-0140-multistream-stacked-reduction-round0/plan.md\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-0140-multistream-stacked-reduction-round0/report.md\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-0140-multistream-stacked-reduction-round0/results/after_apc000.json\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-0140-multistream-stacked-reduction-round0/results/after_apc100.json\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-0140-multist